Spoilers ahead.......
^L
Well, Dr.Jones the archeologist made it to Demigodhood
with 5.7mil. pnts. Yes the same guy who went for a swim
in the moat to get into Croesus' castle only to find his
armour thoroughly rusted and all his scrolls and books
blank.
***************So, what do I recommend?
- teleport control!
- ring of levitation!
- many, I say, many, and I cannot emphasize enough, many
  many, a whole lot of wands of teleportation!
- food! yes lots of food for the endlevel! searching for
  that blasted portal is a pain!
- yes! at least 2 amulets of lifesavings!
- a silver blade (when lawful)
- Excalibur (when lawful)
- a regular sack and two bags of holding.
- I'm telling ya more wands of teleportation.
- use all the wands of digging you can get in hell.
- Ideally an icebox full of cockatrice corpses (couldn't do
  myself, but I sure the hell wished I did).
- Don't forget the darned candles in the mines.
- two blessed spellbooks of magic mapping (or a marker)
- two blessed spellbooks of detect treasure (only if you want points).
- spellbook of knock.
- TINNING KIT! BLESSED! By jove! bless this sucker!
- key
- MAGIC RESISTANCE (endowed by the orb of detection, I believe)
- I'm telling ya, at least 15 wands of teleportation. even that
  wasn't enought, I barely survived the final endlevel.
- SPEEDBOOTS
- Pickaxe! blessed!
****************
    Why all these wands? Teleporting to the Upstairs on the way
back from hell is the fastest way out. ^T is food consuming.
On the advice of a fellow nethacker...ring of levitation helped
avoid the annoying return down two levels etc. each time 'a
mysterious force surrounds you', though I had some trying time.
ESPECIALLY on that hell level full of water, kept on flying back
to it. So many times infact that I had to battle the wizard twice
over there!
    Magic mapping is invaluable for Hell. Detect treasure helps you
avoid looking for them on each level thus saving you alot of time
on each. Do this on the way down. Tin those giants....fastest way
to STR: 18/**. Save those tins for the endlevel! Blessed ones only.
Ending up with a cursed tin opener is too risky (those pesky liches).
    Silver blades cut demons like a hot knife on butter! That includes
Vampires and shades. Excalibur saves your levels and definitely helps
searching for those magic portals.
    2 Bags of holding is good, I wished I had three. One for the 150+
gems. one for all the tins and food. and the last for all those wands
of teleportation. the sack is to protect the bags from getting cursed.
ie. put the bags in the sack after filling them.
    Cockatrice corpes and pickaxes.....the first time it happened to me
I panicked...like Hell. I had bashed the regur...resurrected wizard of
Yendor, he turned to stone. My amulet of Yendor was gone, oh, so
he stole it. I stand by his statue.....NO amulet!!!!!! F*** it was on
the statue! Like crazy I looked for a pickaxe until I met an Elflord.
Then chipped away at the statue, and proceeded back up. You gotta have
both these suckers (and don't forget the gloves). This corpse is the
ultimate weapon in Nethack 3.1 and previous. Note, you must have levi-
tation. Master liches are one of the most annoying creatures in the game
genocide them. They always teleport away when dying and they always
leave things cursed. Otherwise Cockatrice corpse is the answer.
This is the reason why I recommend an icebox...collect those
corpses. When the wizard or the Master Lich creates monsters
around you....bash, bash, bash and they're all statues. Clean,
and quick....no corpses though....so have lots of food. For
points don't do in giants this way.....you lose the gems.
    A good weapon is good, good armour is great....but I think
in all, the best games are done NOT in a hurry. Hack-n-slash
is not always the answer, ESPECIALLY on the way back,
ESPECIALLY ON THE ENDLEVEL.....YOU MAY TELEPORT IN THERE! in
the final level I was getting my butt kicked by 4 minotaurs
created by 4 master liches. I ran out of wand of teleportation,
thank my deity (or the DEV team) for ^T which I used to simply
avoid battle and get to my co-aligned altar. Darn it, it took
me three out of three tries to get to the right one....could
have starved to death one space away from Demigodhood!
    One note about the vibrating space.....make sure all the
artifacts required are not cursed. The order in which they
are used is important. You need not hold them all at once.
And by far, you know things are going alright when no
undead are summoned by your actions. In your attemp be
prepared for a whole lot of trial and errors, ie. many undead
battles **an Army of Darkness*** no pun. I cannot remember exactly
what I did, but the sequence contained six actions not three.
